A||||5||Homicidal||Check out my Pontiac/Fiero inspired 3D Wallpaper I made!!!!!!!||||6||
Z||000000||Homicidal||07-11-2000||04:21 AM||||Titled:  "<B>Road To ?</B>"<P>Inspired by the new Pontiac Grand Prix commercials, some surrealism.  All work was done in Bryce4 and Photoshop 5.0!<P>Sorry, they are a tad big, so I linked them for the high-bandwith impaired!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Here is the original:<BR> <A HREF="http://members.home.net/txi1/Road1.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://members.home.net/txi1/Road1.jpg</A> <P>And the Fiero version: <BR> <A HREF="http://members.home.net/txi1/Road1Fiero.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://members.home.net/txi1/Road1Fiero.jpg</A> <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Whaddya think?<p>[This message has been edited by Homicidal (edited 07-11-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||07-11-2000||02:06 PM||||Cool!<P>I've done a bit of 3D modelling before, mostly landscapes. here are some thumbnails of the images I have on my website..<P>The rest of the pics, as well as full size versions (640 x 480 up to 1024 x 768) are at <A HREF="http://www.digitalfusion.on.ca/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.digitalfusion.on.ca/</A>  in the Free Stuff section..<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.digitalfusion.on.ca/stuff/backgrounds/mountain-lake-sm.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.digitalfusion.on.ca/stuff/backgrounds/water-mountains-sm.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.digitalfusion.on.ca/stuff/backgrounds/water-mountains-snow-sm.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A> ||||reg||10
Z||000002||Homicidal||07-11-2000||02:15 PM||||Gorgeous, what program did you use, 3DSMax?<P>I love Bryce.  Not for it's ease of use, but for it's look.  It's not really good for ultra-fine realistic landscapes, but it does an awesome job at simple Surreal ones, which I LOVE!||||reg||1
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||07-11-2000||05:29 PM||||Thanks..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>I use a program called Terragen to make my landscapes.. it's really simple to use.. but, for the same reason, you can't have any other objects in it like trees etc. so it's only for bare landscapes. The files can be exported to Lightwave though, so you can add in other objects. I don't have a copy of lightwave however, so I haven't tried that yet!<P>I have a few other images I haven't put on the site yet.. but if there's any specific scenes that people might like to see, I'd like to hear sone suggestions.. always looking for new ideas. I'm still learning how to do night scenes.. so none of those yet. I did get some fairly realistic looking scenes with some haze and sunbeams.. I like those ones.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A> ||||reg||10
Z||000004||Homicidal||07-13-2000||03:27 AM||||The only thing I don't like about that Terragen is it's TOO realistic looking!  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||DaRkLoRD||07-13-2000||04:46 AM||||You can still use it to make some pretty far out scenes..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I made some nice ones based on scenes from The Hobbit.. I can't find the images now though, I hope they didn't get deleted...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A> <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
